{"causes": ["The decline of the unified Piast Kingdom of Poland necessitated that many ducal offspring seek alternative paths outside of dynastic marriages.", "The widespread influence of the Dominican Order in Central Europe provided a structured and intellectually vibrant path for aristocratic women seeking religious vocations.", "The establishment of new religious houses was a common practice for medieval nobility to secure spiritual merit and provide for unmarried female relatives."], "effects": ["Euphemia's efforts led to the establishment of the first Dominican convent for women in Racibórz, providing a spiritual and educational institution for the region.", "Her leadership contributed to the consolidation of the Dominican Order's presence and influence within Upper Silesia during the 14th century.", "The convent in Racibórz became a significant center for female religious life and education, impacting the social and cultural landscape of the ducal territory."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "przemyslaw-of-racibrz", "sourceName": "Przemysław of Racibórz", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "euphemia-of-racibrz", "targetName": "Euphemia of Racibórz", "context": "Euphemia of Racibórz's early life and noble status were directly shaped by her father, Duke Przemysław of Racibórz, who died around 1306."}, {"sourceSlug": "euphemia-of-racibrz", "sourceName": "Euphemia of Racibórz", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "dominican-convent-racibrz", "targetName": "Dominican Convent of Racibórz", "context": "Euphemia of Racibórz founded and became the first prioress of the Dominican Convent for women in Racibórz in 1319."}, {"sourceSlug": "dominican-order", "sourceName": "Dominican Order", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "euphemia-of-racibrz", "targetName": "Euphemia of Racibórz", "context": "The spiritual and organizational principles of the Dominican Order profoundly influenced Euphemia of Racibórz's religious vocation and leadership."}, {"sourceSlug": "euphemia-of-